@startuml overview
' cumin-works - one poll of one target repository.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

start
:read .cumin/config.toml of the default branch;
:run the tool checks;
:read the open issues, their labels, sub-issues,\nblockers, pull requests, reviews, and checks;
:skip each issue that cumin cannot read whole\n(notify once);
:decide the actions from the facts\nand from the agents that run;
note right
  The same facts give the same actions.
  The same decision runs right after an agent run ends.
end note
:take the actions that start no agent\n(labels, comments, notifications, merges);
if (a check before agent starts says to stop?) then (yes)
  :start no agent; every issue keeps its state;
else (no)
  :start the agents in the start order,\nup to poll.max_issues_in_progress;
endif
stop

@enduml
